planning_block_quick() {
  local spec_path="${1:-.}"
  local retry_budget="${ACORN_SUBAGENT_RETRY_BUDGET:-1}"
  local retry_backoff="${ACORN_SUBAGENT_RETRY_BACKOFF_SECONDS:-30}"
  local event_path="${ACORN_FAILURE_EVENT_PATH:-}"
  local event_path_display="${event_path:-(unset — events disabled)}"
  local mode="quick"
  case "$retry_budget" in ''|*[!0-9]*) retry_budget=1 ;; esac
  case "$retry_backoff" in ''|*[!0-9]*) retry_backoff=30 ;; esac
  cat <<'METHODOLOGY_EOF' \
    | sed "s|__SPEC_PATH__|${spec_path}|g" \
    | sed "s|__RETRY_BUDGET__|${retry_budget}|g" \
    | sed "s|__RETRY_BACKOFF__|${retry_backoff}|g" \
    | sed "s|__EVENT_PATH_DISPLAY__|${event_path_display}|g" \
    | sed "s|__MODE__|${mode}|g"
## PLANNING METHODOLOGY — MANDATORY INSTRUCTIONS (QUICK MODE)

> **YOU ARE THE ORCHESTRATOR. YOU MUST FOLLOW THIS METHODOLOGY EXACTLY.**
>
> When the user says "let's draft this" (or any variation like "draft it", "start planning", "go", etc.),
> you MUST execute the 2-stage quick pipeline described below.
>
> **DO NOT write a plan yourself. DO NOT skip stages. DO NOT summarize instead of launching agents.**
>
> If you write ANY plan content yourself instead of delegating to sub-agents via the Task tool,
> you have FAILED. Your ONLY job is to launch Task agents and wait for them to finish.

> **RULES FOR SUB-AGENTS (include these in every sub-agent prompt):**
>
> - Sub-agents write ALL work to files using Write/Edit tools
> - Sub-agents return ONLY: `Done. Output: [filepath]`
> - Sub-agents MUST write in chunks of ~4000 tokens max (Write tool, then Edit to append)
> - Sub-agents must NEVER return content, summaries, or explanations to the orchestrator
> - Violation of these rules will blow up the orchestrator's context window

> **VISUAL ASSETS:** The GitHub issue may include images (screenshots, mockups, diagrams) downloaded
> to `__SPEC_PATH__/images/`. Sub-agents should use the Read tool to examine any images when relevant.

---

### Overview

This is the **quick pipeline** — the fastest mode. Recon grounds the spec in the actual codebase,
then a single agent produces SPEC.md directly. Best for straightforward features where speed matters
more than multi-perspective analysis.

You MUST execute these 2 stages in order. Each stage MUST use the Task tool to launch sub-agents.
You MUST NOT skip any stage. You MUST NOT combine stages. You MUST NOT do the work yourself.

0. **Stage 0**: YOU launch 3 parallel Task agents → each explores the codebase from a different angle
1. **Stage 1**: YOU launch 1 Task agent → reads recon + requirements → produces SPEC.md directly

Total: 4 Task agent launches across 2 stages (Stage 0 and Stage 1). No shortcuts.

---

### Stage 0: Codebase Reconnaissance

YOU MUST launch 3 Task tool calls in a SINGLE message (parallel execution). Use model "sonnet".

**Each agent explores the actual codebase to ground all subsequent work in reality.**

**Agent A — Architecture & Structure:**

```
CRITICAL SUB-AGENT INSTRUCTIONS:
- You are the Architecture Reconnaissance agent. You are a SUB-AGENT, not the orchestrator.
- Read the __SPEC_PATH__/PROMPT.md file that the orchestrator provides in your working directory to understand what feature is being planned.
- Explore the actual codebase using Glob, Grep, and Read tools to understand:
  - Directory layout and project structure
  - Tech stack, frameworks, and languages used
  - Build system and deployment model
  - Key entry points and main modules
  - Database schemas and data layer architecture
  - If __SPEC_PATH__/images/ exists, use the Read tool to examine any images for visual context (screenshots, mockups, diagrams)
- Write your findings to __SPEC_PATH__/recon/architecture.md
- Write in chunks of ~4000 tokens maximum. Use Write tool first, then Edit tool to append.
- Focus on FACTS about the codebase, not opinions. Reference specific file paths.
- Your final response must be ONLY: "Done. Output: __SPEC_PATH__/recon/architecture.md"
- Do NOT return any content, summaries, or explanations. ONLY the done message.
```

**Agent B — Relevant Code:**

```
CRITICAL SUB-AGENT INSTRUCTIONS:
- You are the Relevant Code Reconnaissance agent. You are a SUB-AGENT, not the orchestrator.
- Read the __SPEC_PATH__/PROMPT.md file that the orchestrator provides in your working directory to understand what feature is being planned.
- Explore the actual codebase using Glob, Grep, and Read tools to identify:
  - Files and modules most likely to be modified for this feature
  - Existing APIs, endpoints, and interfaces relevant to the feature
  - Data models, types, and schemas that would be affected
  - Integration points with external services or systems
  - Related existing functionality that the feature would interact with
- Write your findings to __SPEC_PATH__/recon/relevant_code.md
- Write in chunks of ~4000 tokens maximum. Use Write tool first, then Edit tool to append.
- Include actual code snippets, function signatures, and type definitions. Reference specific file paths and line numbers.
- Your final response must be ONLY: "Done. Output: __SPEC_PATH__/recon/relevant_code.md"
- Do NOT return any content, summaries, or explanations. ONLY the done message.
```

**Agent C — Conventions & Constraints:**

```
CRITICAL SUB-AGENT INSTRUCTIONS:
- You are the Conventions Reconnaissance agent. You are a SUB-AGENT, not the orchestrator.
- Read the __SPEC_PATH__/PROMPT.md file that the orchestrator provides in your working directory to understand what feature is being planned.
- Explore the actual codebase using Glob, Grep, and Read tools to document:
  - Coding style and naming conventions used throughout
  - Error handling patterns (how errors are thrown, caught, reported)
  - Test framework, test file naming, test patterns and helpers
  - CI/CD configuration and quality gates
  - Dependency management approach
  - Existing abstractions and utilities that should be reused
  - Any CLAUDE.md, AGENTS.md, or contributing guidelines
- Write your findings to __SPEC_PATH__/recon/conventions.md
- Write in chunks of ~4000 tokens maximum. Use Write tool first, then Edit tool to append.
- Include concrete examples from the codebase. Reference specific file paths.
- Your final response must be ONLY: "Done. Output: __SPEC_PATH__/recon/conventions.md"
- Do NOT return any content, summaries, or explanations. ONLY the done message.
```

**After all 3 complete (Recon Completeness Gate):**
Run stage gate via Bash: `acorn _internal validate-stage "__SPEC_PATH__" __MODE__ 0`.
If rc=1, relaunch ONLY failed agent(s), wait `__RETRY_BACKOFF__` seconds between retries, and retry up to `__RETRY_BUDGET__` times per agent.
On exhaustion, run `acorn _internal halt "__SPEC_PATH__" __MODE__ 0 "<agent>" "<artifact>" <halt_reason> "<observed>"` and STOP.
Proceed only if validation exits 0. Do NOT read the files.

---

### Stage 1: Direct Spec

YOU MUST launch 1 Task tool call. Use model "opus".

**A single agent reads all recon and requirements, then produces SPEC.md directly — no intermediaries.**

**Prompt:**

```
CRITICAL SUB-AGENT INSTRUCTIONS:
- You are the Spec Writer. You are a SUB-AGENT, not the orchestrator.
- Read __SPEC_PATH__/PROMPT.md for the full requirements.
- Read __SPEC_PATH__/recon/architecture.md, __SPEC_PATH__/recon/relevant_code.md, and __SPEC_PATH__/recon/conventions.md for codebase context.

Produce a COMPLETE implementation specification. Balance these perspectives:
  1. **Minimal Surgery**: Reuse existing code, touch the fewest files possible.
  2. **Clean Architecture**: Proper separation of concerns where it matters.
  3. **Robustness**: Error handling, validation, edge cases.
  4. **Developer Experience**: Simplicity, clear naming, obvious control flow.

The spec MUST include:

1. **Requirements Traceability Matrix**: For each requirement from the original issue, the exact
   section of this spec that addresses it. Any requirement NOT addressed must be flagged as a gap
   with explicit justification for why it was deferred.

2. **Implementation Plan**: Step-by-step instructions with:
   - Specific file paths and function signatures
   - Data models and schema changes
   - Implementation order with dependencies between steps
   - Each step must be independently verifiable

3. **Testing Strategy**: Grounded in the actual test framework and patterns found in recon.
   - Unit tests, integration tests, and edge case tests
   - Specific test file locations and naming conventions
   - Test data and fixture requirements

4. **Risk Register**: Known risks with severity, likelihood, and mitigation strategies.

5. **Pi Model Recommendation**: Based on the full context of this spec, emit a `## Pi Model Recommendation`
   section at the top of SPEC.md (before ## 1. Requirements Traceability Matrix) containing exactly two lines:

   suggested_pi_model: codex
   suggested_pi_model_rationale: <one-line explanation>

   Use value `codex` when: spec names specific files and functions, implementation is pattern-following,
   touches < 8 files, introduces no new interfaces or schemas, includes explicit test commands.
   Use value `opus` when: requirements are vague or exploratory, introduces new architectural patterns,
   crosses subsystem boundaries, adds new interfaces or schemas, touches > 8 files with design judgment required.

The spec must be ready to be handed to a developer or agent for implementation with ZERO questions.
Be specific — reference actual file paths, function names, and code patterns from the recon documents.

- Write the final spec to __SPEC_PATH__/plans/SPEC.md
- Write in chunks of ~4000 tokens maximum. Use Write tool first, then Edit tool to append.
- Your final response must be ONLY: "Done. Output: __SPEC_PATH__/plans/SPEC.md"
- Do NOT return any content, summaries, or explanations. ONLY the done message.
```

**After completion (Final Stage Gate):**
Run stage gate via Bash: `acorn _internal validate-stage "__SPEC_PATH__" __MODE__ 1`.
If rc=1, relaunch ONLY failed agent(s), wait `__RETRY_BACKOFF__` seconds between retries, and retry up to `__RETRY_BUDGET__` times per agent.
On exhaustion, run `acorn _internal halt "__SPEC_PATH__" __MODE__ 1 "<agent>" "<artifact>" <halt_reason> "<observed>"` and STOP.
When validation exits 0, read __SPEC_PATH__/plans/SPEC.md and present it to the user. This is the ONLY file you read.

---

### Orchestrator Context Management — CRITICAL

**Your context is precious. Sub-agents have their own 200k token contexts. You do NOT.**

- Your ONLY job is to launch Task agents and confirm they completed. That's it.
- You need ~1k tokens per stage. If your context grows beyond ~10k tokens, you broke a rule.
- NEVER read sub-agent output files yourself (the ONLY exception: __SPEC_PATH__/plans/SPEC.md at the very end)
- NEVER consume sub-agent return messages beyond confirming the word "Done"
- NEVER write plan content yourself — that's what the 4 sub-agents are for
- If validate-stage returns non-zero, relaunch ONLY failed agent(s), wait __RETRY_BACKOFF__ seconds, and retry up to __RETRY_BUDGET__ times per agent. On exhaustion run `acorn _internal halt ...` and STOP. Do NOT do failed work yourself as fallback.
METHODOLOGY_EOF
}

planning_block_clarify() {
  local spec_path="${1:-.}"
  local mode="${2:-lite}"
  cat <<'CLARIFY_BLOCK' \
    | sed "s|__SPEC_PATH__|${spec_path}|g" \
    | sed "s|__MODE__|${mode}|g"
## PRE-STAGE: /clarify (M37 substrate-critical check)

**MANDATORY BEFORE STAGE 0 RECON.**

### M37 substrate-critical heuristics

- **H1**: Builds mechanical enforcement infrastructure (gates, validators, schemas)
- **H2**: Defines shared contracts used by >=2 downstream capabilities
- **H3**: Establishes persistent state structures (state machines, event logs)
- **H4**: Future capabilities depend on this shipping first (foundational enabler)
- **H5**: Failure cascades across multiple systems

### MVP scope clarification questions

1. What is the MINIMUM VIABLE function this spec ships?
2. What is the FULL design (all functionality this spec's domain encompasses)?
3. What is DEFERRED to expansion passes? (Enumerate explicit list)
4. What architectural patterns support expansion? (Interfaces, plugins, strategies, extensible types, forward-compatible enums)
5. What is the LANDING capability for deferred work? (Specific future capability or epic)

### Execution

1. Write `__SPEC_PATH__/clarifications.input.json`:

```json
{
  "mode": "__MODE__",
  "heuristics_fired": ["H2", "H4"],
  "mvp_scope": "...",
  "full_design": "...",
  "deferred": ["item 1", "item 2"],
  "arch_patterns": "...",
  "landing_capability": "Cap G-1"
}
```

2. Render `clarifications.md`:

```bash
PYTHONPATH=. python3 -m runtime.acorn.stages.clarify \
  --spec-dir "__SPEC_PATH__" \
  --input "__SPEC_PATH__/clarifications.input.json"
```

3. Run stage gate:

```bash
acorn _internal validate-stage "__SPEC_PATH__" __MODE__ pre0
```

On exhaustion (M29 hard-limit), run:

```bash
acorn _internal halt "__SPEC_PATH__" __MODE__ pre0 clarify \
  clarifications.md CLARIFY_FAILED "validate-stage returned 1"
```

Do NOT proceed to Stage 0 until pre0 passes.

---
CLARIFY_BLOCK
}

render_comments_block() {
  local issue_json="$1"
  printf '%s\n' "$issue_json" | jq -r '
    if (.comments | length) == 0 then
      "_No discussion comments yet._"
    else
      .comments[] |
      "### Comment by @\(.author.login // "unknown") on \(.updatedAt // .createdAt // "unknown-time")\n\n\(.body // "")\n"
    end
  '
}

render_prompt_md() {
  local issue_title="$1"
  local issue_body="$2"
  local issue_json="$3"
  local out_tmp="$4"
  local mode="${5:-full}"
  local spec_path="${6:-.}"
  local url_mapping_file="${7:-}"
  local output_mode="${8:-single}"

  # Rewrite image URLs in body if mapping exists
  if [ -n "$url_mapping_file" ] && [ -f "$url_mapping_file" ] && [ -s "$url_mapping_file" ]; then
    issue_body="$(rewrite_image_urls_in_text "$issue_body" "$url_mapping_file")"
  fi

  {
    printf '# Feature Spec: %s\n\n' "$issue_title"
    printf '## Requirements\n\n'
    if [ -n "$issue_body" ]; then
      printf '%s\n\n' "$issue_body"
    else
      printf '_No issue body provided._\n\n'
    fi

    printf '## Discussion / Context\n\n'
    local comments_text
    comments_text="$(render_comments_block "$issue_json")"
    if [ -n "$url_mapping_file" ] && [ -f "$url_mapping_file" ] && [ -s "$url_mapping_file" ]; then
      comments_text="$(rewrite_image_urls_in_text "$comments_text" "$url_mapping_file")"
    fi
    printf '%s' "$comments_text"
    printf '\n---\n\n'

    if [ "${ACORN_CLARIFY_ENABLED:-0}" = "1" ]; then
      planning_block_clarify "$spec_path" "$mode"
    fi

    planning_block "$mode" "$spec_path"

    if [ "$output_mode" = "three-artifact" ]; then
      cat <<EOF

---

### THREE-ARTIFACT OUTPUT MODE (ACORN_OUTPUT_MODE=three-artifact)

IMPORTANT: This OVERRIDES the prior "Your final response must be ONLY..." instruction.
Produce THREE files in ${spec_path}/plans/: SPEC.md, PLAN.md, TASKS.md.

PLAN.md required headings (exact order):
## 1. Architecture Decisions
## 2. API Contracts
## 3. Data Model Changes
## 4. Implementation Sequence
## 5. Risk Register

TASKS.md format:
- first line exactly: # acorn-tasks-schema: v1
- then YAML tasks with keys: id, title, size (XS/S/M/L/XL), files, verify, depends_on
- XL tasks (>8 files OR >3 interfaces) include: ⚠️ XL: requires decomposition
- verify commands runnable from repo root (no implicit cd)

SPEC.md in this mode should stay stand-alone and functional, while implementation/testing detail moves to PLAN.md/TASKS.md.

Final response in this mode MUST be exactly:
Done. Output: ${spec_path}/plans/SPEC.md + ${spec_path}/plans/PLAN.md + ${spec_path}/plans/TASKS.md
EOF
    fi

    printf '\n\n---\n\n'
    cat <<'EOF'
## Completion Protocol

When implementation is complete, the implementing agent must:

1. Create or update `DONE.md` in the spec directory (`.specs/<slug>/DONE.md`).
   **IMPORTANT**: Always write to the spec directory, NOT the worktree root.
   For non-repo work (scripts, config, behavioral specs), the spec directory
   is at `<project_root>/<repo>/main/.specs/<slug>/DONE.md`.
2. Include the exact test commands run and their outcomes.
3. For non-repo work, include a `## Work Type` section listing the category
   and primary artifact paths.
4. Summarize file changes and rationale in concise bullet points.
5. List any follow-up risks or deferred work.
EOF
  } > "$out_tmp"
}

validate_prompt_md() {
  local prompt_path="$1"
  local output_mode="${2:-single}"
  grep -q 'PLANNING METHODOLOGY — MANDATORY INSTRUCTIONS' "$prompt_path" || return 1
  if [ "$output_mode" = "three-artifact" ]; then
    grep -q 'THREE-ARTIFACT OUTPUT MODE' "$prompt_path" || return 1
  fi
  if grep -E -q '__SPEC_PATH__|__RETRY_BUDGET__|__RETRY_BACKOFF__|__EVENT_PATH_DISPLAY__|__MODE__' "$prompt_path"; then
    return 1
  fi

  # Enforcement hook (forge#262 /clarify pre-stage): fail loudly when enabled
  # but pre-stage section/commands are missing from rendered PROMPT.md.
  if [ "${ACORN_CLARIFY_ENABLED:-0}" = "1" ]; then
    grep -q '## PRE-STAGE: /clarify (M37 substrate-critical check)' "$prompt_path" || return 1
    grep -q 'PYTHONPATH=. python3 -m runtime.acorn.stages.clarify' "$prompt_path" || return 1
    grep -E -q 'acorn _internal validate-stage ".*" (full|lite|quick) pre0' "$prompt_path" || return 1
  fi

  return 0
}

get_extension_from_url() {
  local url="$1"
  # Strip query parameters and fragments
  local path="${url%%\?*}"
  path="${path%%#*}"
  # Extract extension
  local ext="${path##*.}"
  # Lowercase
  ext="$(printf '%s' "$ext" | tr '[:upper:]' '[:lower:]')"
  case "$ext" in
    png|jpg|jpeg|gif|webp|svg) printf '%s' "$ext" ;;
    *) printf 'png' ;;
  esac
}

generate_image_filename() {
  local url="$1"
  local ext
  ext="$(get_extension_from_url "$url")"

  local hash
  if command -v md5 >/dev/null 2>&1; then
    hash="$(printf '%s' "$url" | md5)"
  elif command -v md5sum >/dev/null 2>&1; then
    hash="$(printf '%s' "$url" | md5sum | cut -d' ' -f1)"
  else
    hash="$(printf '%s' "$url" | cksum | cut -d' ' -f1)"
  fi

  printf '%s.%s' "$hash" "$ext"
}

extract_image_urls() {
  local issue_json="$1"

  # Combine body and all comment bodies into a text stream
  local all_text
  all_text="$(printf '%s' "$issue_json" | jq -r '
    [.body // ""] + [(.comments // [])[] | .body // ""]
    | .[]
  ')" || true

  [ -z "$all_text" ] && return 0

  {
    # Strategy 1: Standard image URLs with known extensions
    printf '%s' "$all_text" \
      | grep -oE '!\[[^]]*\]\([^)]+\)' \
      | sed -nE 's/.*\(([^ ")]+).*/\1/p' \
      | grep -iE '\.(png|jpe?g|gif|webp|svg)(\?[^[:space:]]*)?$' \
      || true

    # Strategy 2: GitHub asset UUID URLs (no extension)
    printf '%s' "$all_text" \
      | grep -oE '!\[[^]]*\]\([^)]+\)' \
      | sed -nE 's/.*\(([^ ")]+).*/\1/p' \
      | grep -E '^https://(github\.com/.*/assets/[0-9a-f-]+|private-user-images\.githubusercontent\.com/)' \
      || true
  } | sort -u
}

extract_and_download_images() {
  local issue_json="$1"
  local images_dir="$2"

  require_cmds curl

  local mapping_file
  mapping_file="$(mktemp)"

  mkdir -p "$images_dir"

  local urls
  urls="$(extract_image_urls "$issue_json")"

  if [ -z "$urls" ]; then
    info "No images found in issue" >&2
    printf '%s' "$mapping_file"
    return 0
  fi

  local url count=0 success=0
  while IFS= read -r url; do
    [ -n "$url" ] || continue
    count=$((count + 1))

    local filename
    filename="$(generate_image_filename "$url")"
    local output_path="$images_dir/$filename"
    local relative_path="images/$filename"

    # Skip if already downloaded (idempotent)
    if [ -f "$output_path" ] && [ -s "$output_path" ]; then
      info "Image already exists: $relative_path" >&2
      printf '%s\t%s\n' "$url" "$relative_path" >> "$mapping_file"
      success=$((success + 1))
      continue
    fi

    # Download to temp file first, then move (atomic)
    local tmp_download="$output_path.tmp"
    if curl -fsSL --max-time 30 --retry 2 -o "$tmp_download" "$url" 2>/dev/null; then
      if [ -s "$tmp_download" ]; then
        mv "$tmp_download" "$output_path"
        info "Downloaded: $relative_path" >&2
        printf '%s\t%s\n' "$url" "$relative_path" >> "$mapping_file"
        success=$((success + 1))
      else
        warn "Downloaded file is empty: $url"
        rm -f "$tmp_download"
      fi
    else
      warn "Failed to download image: $url (keeping original URL)"
      rm -f "$tmp_download"
    fi
  done <<< "$urls"

  info "Images: $success/$count downloaded successfully" >&2
  printf '%s' "$mapping_file"
}

rewrite_image_urls_in_text() {
  local text="$1"
  local mapping_file="$2"

  # Return text unchanged if no mapping
  [ -n "$mapping_file" ] && [ -f "$mapping_file" ] && [ -s "$mapping_file" ] || {
    printf '%s' "$text"
    return 0
  }

  local result="$text"
  local original_url local_path
  while IFS=$'\t' read -r original_url local_path; do
    [ -n "$original_url" ] || continue
    # Use bash string replacement -- no sed escaping needed
    result="${result//"$original_url"/$local_path}"
  done < "$mapping_file"

  printf '%s' "$result"
}

start_session() {
  local repo="$1"
  local slug="$2"
  local spec_path="$3"
  local auto_trigger="${4:-0}"
  local session_name
  session_name="$(canonical_session_name "$repo" "$slug")"

  require_cmds tmux claude

  if tmux has-session -t "$session_name" 2>/dev/null; then
    printf '%s\n%s' "tmux" "$session_name"
    return 0
  fi

  tmux new-session -d -s "$session_name" -c "$spec_path"
  if [ "$auto_trigger" -eq 1 ]; then
    tmux send-keys -t "$session_name" "claude --dangerously-skip-permissions" C-m || true
  else
    tmux send-keys -t "$session_name" "claude" C-m || true
  fi
  printf '%s\n%s' "tmux" "$session_name"
}

# Wait for Claude Code to show its input prompt in a tmux session.
# Polls tmux pane content at regular intervals up to a maximum wait time.
# Returns 0 when the prompt is detected, 1 on timeout.
# On timeout the caller should proceed anyway (graceful degradation).
wait_for_claude_ready() {
  local session_name="$1"
  local max_wait="${2:-30}"
  local interval="${3:-2}"
  local elapsed=0

  while [ "$elapsed" -lt "$max_wait" ]; do
    local pane_content
    pane_content="$(tmux capture-pane -t "$session_name" -ep 2>/dev/null || true)"
    # Strip any residual ANSI escape codes
    pane_content="$(printf '%s' "$pane_content" | sed 's/\x1b\[[0-9;]*[a-zA-Z]//g')"
    # Check the last few lines for Claude Code's prompt
    if printf '%s' "$pane_content" | tail -n5 | grep -qE '>\s*$'; then
      return 0
    fi
    sleep "$interval"
    elapsed=$((elapsed + interval))
  done

  return 1
}

# Send auto-trigger message to a claude session once it is ready.
# Waits for Claude Code to show its input prompt, then sends the message.
# Falls back to sending after timeout if prompt is not detected.
send_auto_trigger() {
  local session_name="$1"
  local message="$2"
  (
    # Wait for Claude Code to be ready (up to 30s); proceed on timeout (|| true
    # prevents set -e from killing the subshell when wait_for_claude_ready returns 1)
    wait_for_claude_ready "$session_name" 30 2 || true
    tmux send-keys -t "$session_name" -l "$message"
    sleep 1
    tmux send-keys -t "$session_name" Enter
  ) &
  disown
}

kill_session() {
  local backend="$1"
  local session_name="$2"
  local repo="$3"
  local slug="$4"

  if [ -n "$session_name" ] && command -v tmux >/dev/null 2>&1; then
    if tmux has-session -t "$session_name" 2>/dev/null; then
      tmux kill-session -t "$session_name" >/dev/null 2>&1 || warn "Failed to kill session $session_name"
      return 0
    fi
  fi

  if command -v tmux >/dev/null 2>&1; then
    local candidates
    candidates="$(tmux list-sessions -F '#S' 2>/dev/null | grep -E "(acorn:${repo}:${slug}|${repo}_specs_${slug}_(claude|pi))" || true)"
    if [ -n "$candidates" ]; then
      while IFS= read -r s; do
        [ -n "$s" ] || continue
        tmux kill-session -t "$s" >/dev/null 2>&1 || warn "Failed killing fallback session $s"
      done <<< "$candidates"
    else
      warn "No active session found for $slug"
    fi
  fi
}

session_state() {
  local session_name="$1"
  local has_meta="$2"

  if [ -z "$session_name" ]; then
    printf 'no-session'
    return 0
  fi

  if ! command -v tmux >/dev/null 2>&1; then
    printf 'unknown'
    return 0
  fi

  if tmux has-session -t "$session_name" 2>/dev/null; then
    printf 'running'
  elif [ "$has_meta" -eq 1 ]; then
    printf 'dead'
  else
    printf 'no-session'
  fi
}

attach_command() {
  local session_name="$1"
  local state="$2"

  if [ "$state" = "running" ]; then
    printf 'tmux attach -t %s' "$session_name"
  else
    printf '%s' "—"
  fi
}

write_meta_json() {
  local path="$1"
  local repo="$2"
  local issue_number="$3"
  local issue_title="$4"
  local slug="$5"
  local backend="$6"
  local session_name="$7"
  local mode="${8:-full}"
  local output_mode="${9:-single}"

  local ts
  ts="$(date -u +"%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ")"

  local clarify_run
  if [ "${ACORN_CLARIFY_ENABLED:-0}" = "1" ]; then
    clarify_run=true
  else
    clarify_run=false
  fi

  jq -n \
    --arg repo "$repo" \
    --argjson issue_number "$issue_number" \
    --arg issue_title "$issue_title" \
    --arg slug "$slug" \
    --arg created_at "$ts" \
    --arg session_backend "$backend" \
    --arg session_name "$session_name" \
    --arg mode "$mode" \
    --arg output_mode "$output_mode" \
    --argjson clarify_run "$clarify_run" \
    '{repo:$repo, issue_number:$issue_number, issue_title:$issue_title, slug:$slug, created_at:$created_at, session_backend:$session_backend, session_name:$session_name, mode:$mode, output_mode:$output_mode, clarify_run:$clarify_run}' \
    > "$path"
}

file_mtime_epoch() {
  local path="$1"
  if stat -f '%m' "$path" >/dev/null 2>&1; then
    stat -f '%m' "$path"
  else
    stat -c '%Y' "$path"
  fi
}

human_age() {
  local epoch="$1"
  local now
  now="$(date +%s)"
  local diff=$((now - epoch))
  if [ "$diff" -lt 60 ]; then
    printf '%ss' "$diff"
  elif [ "$diff" -lt 3600 ]; then
    printf '%sm' $((diff / 60))
  elif [ "$diff" -lt 86400 ]; then
    printf '%sh' $((diff / 3600))
  else
    printf '%sd' $((diff / 86400))
  fi
}

status_for_spec() {
  local repo_main="$1"
  local issue_number="$2"
  local spec_path="$3"
  local halted=0
  [ -f "$spec_path/recon/HALT.md" ] && halted=1
  [ -f "$spec_path/plans/HALT.md" ] && halted=1
  local prefix=""
  [ "$halted" -eq 1 ] && prefix='[HALTED] '

  local labels_json='[]'
  if [ -n "$issue_number" ]; then
    local _nwo
    _nwo="$(gh_repo_nwo "$repo_main")"
    labels_json="$(gh issue view "$issue_number" --repo "$_nwo" --json labels 2>/dev/null | jq -c '.labels // []')" || true
  fi

  # Return the actual lifecycle label if present.
  local label found=""
  for label in "${LIFECYCLE_LABELS[@]}"; do
    if printf '%s' "$labels_json" | jq -e --arg l "$label" '.[] | select(.name == $l)' >/dev/null 2>&1; then
      found="$label"
      break
    fi
  done

  if [ -n "$found" ]; then
    printf '%s%s' "$prefix" "$found"
  else
    # Backward-compatible fallback for older unlabeled issues.
    local final_exists=0
    local prompt_exists=0
    [ -f "$spec_path/plans/SPEC.md" ] && final_exists=1
    [ -f "$spec_path/PROMPT.md" ] && prompt_exists=1

    if [ "$final_exists" -eq 1 ]; then
      printf '%sreview' "$prefix"
    elif [ "$prompt_exists" -eq 1 ]; then
      printf '%splanning' "$prefix"
    else
      printf '%sunknown' "$prefix"
    fi
  fi
}

clarification_for_issue() {
  local repo_main="$1"
  local issue_number="$2"

  [ -n "$issue_number" ] || { printf -- '--'; return 0; }

  local labels_json _nwo2
  _nwo2="$(gh_repo_nwo "$repo_main")"
  labels_json="$(gh issue view "$issue_number" --repo "$_nwo2" --json labels 2>/dev/null | jq -c '.labels // []')" \
    || { printf -- '--'; return 0; }

  if printf '%s' "$labels_json" | jq -e '.[] | select(.name == "human-clarified")' >/dev/null 2>&1; then
    printf 'clarified'
  elif printf '%s' "$labels_json" | jq -e '.[] | select(.name == "ai-drafted")' >/dev/null 2>&1; then
    printf 'ai-drafted'
  else
    printf -- '--'
  fi
}

print_list_header() {
  printf '%-16s %-8s %-40s %-18s %-6s %-8s %-11s %-6s %s\n' "repo" "issue" "slug" "status" "mode" "age" "clarify" "deps" "spec_path"
}

print_list_row() {
  local repo="$1"
  local issue="$2"
  local slug="$3"
  local status="$4"
  local mode="$5"
  local age="$6"
  local clarify="$7"
  local deps="$8"
  local path="$9"
  printf '%-16s %-8s %-40s %-18s %-6s %-8s %-11s %-6s %s\n' "$repo" "$issue" "$slug" "$status" "$mode" "$age" "$clarify" "$deps" "$path"
}

print_status_header() {
  printf '%-16s %-42s %-12s %-8s %-18s %s\n' \
    "REPO" "SLUG" "SESSION" "BACKEND" "STATUS" "ATTACH"
}

print_status_row() {
  local repo="$1"
  local slug="$2"
  local session="$3"
  local backend="$4"
  local status="$5"
  local attach="$6"
  printf '%-16s %-42s %-12s %-8s %-18s %s\n' \
    "$repo" "$slug" "$session" "$backend" "$status" "$attach"
}

list_specs_for_repo() {
  local repo="$1"
  local repo_main
  repo_main="$(safe_repo_main "$repo")"

  local root
  root="$(spec_root "$repo")"
  [ -d "$root" ] || return 0

  local dir
  for dir in "$root"/*; do
    [ -d "$dir" ] || continue
    local slug
    slug="$(basename "$dir")"
    local issue
    issue="$(issue_number_from_slug "$slug")"
    local status
    status="$(status_for_spec "$repo_main" "$issue" "$dir")"
    local clarify
    clarify="$(clarification_for_issue "$repo_main" "$issue")"
    local mode="full"
    if [ -f "$dir/meta.json" ]; then
      mode="$(jq -r '.mode // "full"' "$dir/meta.json" 2>/dev/null || printf 'full')"
    fi
    local age
    age="$(human_age "$(file_mtime_epoch "$dir")")"
    local deps="--"
    if [ "$_SHOW_DEPS" -eq 1 ] && [ -n "$issue" ] && [ "$issue" != "?" ]; then
      local _list_nwo
      _list_nwo="${_LIST_NWO:-}"
      if [ -z "$_list_nwo" ]; then
        _list_nwo="$(gh_repo_nwo "$repo_main" 2>/dev/null || true)"
        _LIST_NWO="$_list_nwo"
      fi
      if [ -n "$_list_nwo" ]; then
        local dep_count
        dep_count="$(blocked_by_count "$repo_main" "$issue" "$_list_nwo" 2>/dev/null || printf '0')"
        if [ "$dep_count" -gt 0 ] 2>/dev/null; then
          deps="$dep_count"
        fi
      fi
    fi
    print_list_row "$repo" "${issue:-?}" "$slug" "$status" "$mode" "$age" "$clarify" "$deps" "$dir"
  done
}

list_specs_all() {
  local main_dir
  for main_dir in "$PROJECTS_DIR"/*/main; do
    [ -d "$main_dir" ] || continue
    local repo
    repo="$(basename "$(dirname "$main_dir")")"
    if [ -d "$main_dir/.specs" ]; then
      list_specs_for_repo "$repo"
    fi
  done
}

list_status_for_repo() {
  local repo="$1"
  local repo_main
  repo_main="$(safe_repo_main "$repo")"

  local root
  root="$(spec_root "$repo")"
  [ -d "$root" ] || return 0

  local dir
  for dir in "$root"/*; do
    [ -d "$dir" ] || continue

    local slug
    slug="$(basename "$dir")"

    local session_name="" backend="tmux" has_meta=0
    if [ -f "$dir/meta.json" ]; then
      has_meta=1
      session_name="$(jq -r '.session_name // ""' "$dir/meta.json" 2>/dev/null || true)"
      backend="$(jq -r '.session_backend // "tmux"' "$dir/meta.json" 2>/dev/null || true)"
    fi

    [ -n "$backend" ] && [ "$backend" != "null" ] || backend="tmux"

    if [ -z "$session_name" ] || [ "$session_name" = "null" ]; then
      session_name="$(canonical_session_name "$repo" "$slug")"
    fi

    local state
    state="$(session_state "$session_name" "$has_meta")"

    local issue
    issue="$(issue_number_from_slug "$slug")"
    local pipeline_status
    pipeline_status="$(status_for_spec "$repo_main" "$issue" "$dir")"

    local attach
    attach="$(attach_command "$session_name" "$state")"

    local display_slug
    display_slug="$(truncate_str "$slug" 40)"

    print_status_row "$repo" "$display_slug" "$state" "$backend" "$pipeline_status" "$attach"
  done
}

list_status_all() {
  local main_dir
  for main_dir in "$PROJECTS_DIR"/*/main; do
    [ -d "$main_dir" ] || continue
    local repo
    repo="$(basename "$(dirname "$main_dir")")"
    if [ -d "$main_dir/.specs" ]; then
      list_status_for_repo "$repo"
    fi
  done
}

cmd_create() {
  local repo="$1"
  local issue_number="$2"
  shift 2

  local auto_trigger=1
  local mode="full"
  while [ "$#" -gt 0 ]; do
    case "$1" in
      --no-auto)
        auto_trigger=0
        ;;
      --lite)
        [ "$mode" = "full" ] || die "--lite and --quick are mutually exclusive"
        mode="lite"
        ;;
      --quick)
        [ "$mode" = "full" ] || die "--lite and --quick are mutually exclusive"
        mode="quick"
        ;;
      *)
        die "Unknown option for create: $1"
        ;;
    esac
    shift
  done

  # Forge: auth pre-flight gate
  local auth_check="${FOREMAN_HOME:-$HOME/.foreman}/bin/auth-check"".sh"
  if [ -x "$auth_check" ]; then
    if ! "$auth_check" --quiet 2>&1; then
      die "Auth pre-flight failed; run "$auth_check" manually to diagnose."
    fi
  fi

  # Forge: circuit-breaker check
  if ! check_circuit_breaker; then
    die "Circuit breaker tripped — refusing to launch new session"
  fi

  require_cmds gh jq tmux claude
  local repo_main
  repo_main="$(safe_repo_main "$repo")"

  info "Fetching issue #$issue_number"
  local issue_json
  issue_json="$(gh_issue_json "$repo_main" "$issue_number")" || die "Failed to fetch issue #$issue_number"

  local title body slug root dir
  title="$(printf '%s' "$issue_json" | jq -r '.title // "Untitled issue"')"
  body="$(printf '%s' "$issue_json" | jq -r '.body // ""')"
  slug="$(build_slug "$issue_number" "$title")"
  root="$(spec_root "$repo")"
  dir="$(spec_dir "$repo" "$slug")"

  local output_mode="${ACORN_OUTPUT_MODE:-single}"
  case "$output_mode" in
    single|three-artifact) ;;
    *)
      warn "Unknown ACORN_OUTPUT_MODE=$output_mode; falling back to single"
      output_mode="single"
      ;;
  esac

  mkdir -p "$dir/plans"
  mkdir -p "$dir/recon"
  mkdir -p "$dir/images"

  local prompt_path="$dir/PROMPT.md"
  if [ ! -f "$prompt_path" ]; then
    # Extract and download images from issue markdown
    info "Extracting images from issue #$issue_number"
    local url_mapping_file
    url_mapping_file="$(extract_and_download_images "$issue_json" "$dir/images")"

    local tmp_path="$prompt_path.tmp"
    render_prompt_md "$title" "$body" "$issue_json" "$tmp_path" "$mode" "$dir" "$url_mapping_file" "$output_mode"
    if ! validate_prompt_md "$tmp_path" "$output_mode"; then
      rm -f "$tmp_path"
      rm -f "$url_mapping_file"
      die "Prompt generation failed: planning anchor missing"
    fi
    mv "$tmp_path" "$prompt_path"
    rm -f "$url_mapping_file"
    info "Generated $prompt_path"
  else
    local recorded_om
    if recorded_om="$(jq -r '.output_mode // "single"' "$dir/meta.json" 2>/dev/null)"; then
      :
    else
      recorded_om="single"
    fi
    if [ "$recorded_om" != "$output_mode" ]; then
      warn "PROMPT.md exists with output_mode=$recorded_om but env requests $output_mode"
      warn "PROMPT.md will NOT be regenerated. Delete $dir/PROMPT.md and re-run create to switch modes."
      output_mode="$recorded_om"
    fi
    info "PROMPT.md already exists, leaving as-is"
  fi

  _emit_pi_ship_warning "$repo" "$slug" "$body"

  ensure_labels "$repo_main"
  set_issue_state_label "$repo_main" "$issue_number" "spec-in-progress"

  comment_issue "$repo_main" "$issue_number" "Spec started locally at: $dir"

  local session_name
  local meta_path="$dir/meta.json"
  session_name=""

  if [ -f "$meta_path" ]; then
    session_name="$(jq -r '.session_name // ""' "$meta_path" 2>/dev/null || true)"
  fi

  local alive=0
  local started_new_session=0
  if [ -n "$session_name" ] && command -v tmux >/dev/null 2>&1; then
    if tmux has-session -t "$session_name" 2>/dev/null; then
      alive=1
    fi
  fi

  if [ "$alive" -eq 0 ]; then
    local session_result
    session_result="$(start_session "$repo" "$slug" "$dir" "$auto_trigger")"
    session_name="$(printf '%s' "$session_result" | tail -n1)"
    started_new_session=1

    if [ "$auto_trigger" -eq 1 ]; then
      send_auto_trigger "$session_name" "$(auto_trigger_message "$dir" "$mode")"
      info "Auto-trigger queued (waiting for readiness, up to ~30s)"
    fi

    # Forge: record session launch for watchdog
    local watchdog_state="${FOREMAN_HOME:-$HOME/.foreman}/watchdog-state"
    if [ -d "$watchdog_state" ]; then
      date -Iseconds > "$watchdog_state/launch_${session_name}" 2>/dev/null || true
    fi

    # Forge: register session with forged daemon
    register_with_forged "$session_name" "$mode" "$dir"
  fi

  write_meta_json "$meta_path" "$repo" "$issue_number" "$title" "$slug" "tmux" "$session_name" "$mode" "$output_mode"
  jq -e '(.output_mode == "single") or (.output_mode == "three-artifact")' "$meta_path" >/dev/null 2>&1 || die "Failed to write valid meta.json output_mode"

  echo ""
  echo "Created spec: $dir"
  echo "Mode: $mode"
  echo "Output mode: $output_mode"
  echo "Session: $session_name"
  echo "Attach: tmux attach -t $session_name"
  if [ "$auto_trigger" -eq 1 ]; then
    if [ "$started_new_session" -eq 1 ]; then
      echo "Auto-trigger: waiting for Claude Code to be ready (up to ~30s)"
    else
      echo "Auto-trigger: skipped (session already running)"
    fi
  else
    echo "Auto-trigger: disabled (--no-auto)"
    echo "Manual trigger: say \"let's draft this\" in the planning session"
  fi

  notify_telegram "acorn: spec pipeline started for #${issue_number} (${slug}) [${mode}]"
  # auth-check.sh gate intentionally lives in cmd_create.
}

cmd_list()
{
  local repo=""
  _SHOW_DEPS=0
  _LIST_NWO=""

  while [ "$#" -gt 0 ]; do
    case "$1" in
      --deps)
        _SHOW_DEPS=1
        ;;
      *)
        repo="$1"
        ;;
    esac
    shift
  done

  require_cmds gh jq
  print_list_header
  if [ -n "$repo" ]; then
    list_specs_for_repo "$repo"
  else
    list_specs_all
  fi

  _SHOW_DEPS=0
  _LIST_NWO=""
}

cmd_status() {
  local repo="${1:-}"
  require_cmds jq
  print_status_header
  if [ -n "$repo" ]; then
    list_status_for_repo "$repo"
  else
    list_status_all
  fi
}

# commit_spec_dir(slug, repo_main) -- commit .specs/<slug>/ on ${ACORN_COMMIT_BRANCH:-main}.
# Captures caller branch and restores on success and failure paths. Idempotent.
# Pathspec-limited so unrelated dirty/staged files are NEVER swept in.
commit_spec_dir() {
  local slug="$1"
  local repo_main="$2"
  local rel=".specs/${slug}"
  local target_branch="${ACORN_COMMIT_BRANCH:-main}"

  [ -d "$repo_main/$rel" ] || die "spec dir not found: $repo_main/$rel"

  local original_branch
  original_branch="$(cd "$repo_main" && git symbolic-ref --quiet --short HEAD)" \
    || die "repo_main is in detached HEAD; refusing to commit"

  info "Attempting to commit $rel on branch $target_branch (caller was on $original_branch)"

  # Explicit `|| exit N` per operation. Bash's `set -e` is unreliable inside
  # subshells (varies between if/then nesting and conditional contexts), so
  # control flow is explicit. Distinguishable exit codes aid diagnosis.
  local rc=0
  set +e
  (
    cd "$repo_main" || exit 100
    if [ "$original_branch" != "$target_branch" ]; then
      git checkout "$target_branch" || exit 101
    fi
    if git diff --quiet -- "$rel" \
       && git diff --cached --quiet -- "$rel" \
       && [ -z "$(git ls-files --others --exclude-standard -- "$rel")" ]; then
      info "$rel already committed (idempotent skip)"
      exit 0
    fi
    git add -- "$rel" || exit 102
    git commit -m "spec: commit ${slug} for dispatch (acorn approve)" -- "$rel" || exit 103
    info "Committed $rel on branch $target_branch"
  )
  rc=$?
  set -e

  if [ "$original_branch" != "$target_branch" ]; then
    set +e
    ( cd "$repo_main" && git checkout "$original_branch" )
    local restore_rc=$?
    set -e
    [ "$restore_rc" -eq 0 ] || warn "Failed to restore branch $original_branch on $repo_main; manual intervention may be needed"
  fi

  [ "$rc" -eq 0 ] || die "commit_spec_dir failed for $rel (rc=$rc)"
}

# commit_spec_dir_on_branch(slug, repo_main, target_branch) -- --orphan-branch variant.
# Creates target_branch if missing. Always restores caller branch.
commit_spec_dir_on_branch() {
  local slug="$1"
  local repo_main="$2"
  local target_branch="$3"
  local rel=".specs/${slug}"

  [ -n "$target_branch" ] || die "commit_spec_dir_on_branch: target_branch is required"
  [ -d "$repo_main/$rel" ] || die "spec dir not found: $repo_main/$rel"

  local original_branch
  original_branch="$(cd "$repo_main" && git symbolic-ref --quiet --short HEAD)" \
    || die "repo_main is in detached HEAD; refusing to commit"

  info "Attempting to commit $rel on orphan branch $target_branch (caller was on $original_branch)"

  local rc=0
  set +e
  (
    cd "$repo_main" || exit 100
    if git show-ref --verify --quiet "refs/heads/$target_branch"; then
      git checkout "$target_branch" || exit 101
    else
      git checkout -b "$target_branch" || exit 101
    fi
    if git diff --quiet -- "$rel" \
       && git diff --cached --quiet -- "$rel" \
       && [ -z "$(git ls-files --others --exclude-standard -- "$rel")" ]; then
      info "$rel already committed on $target_branch (idempotent skip)"
      exit 0
    fi
    git add -- "$rel" || exit 102
    git commit -m "spec: commit ${slug} for dispatch (acorn approve)" -- "$rel" || exit 103
    info "Committed $rel on orphan branch $target_branch"
  )
  rc=$?
  set -e

  set +e
  ( cd "$repo_main" && git checkout "$original_branch" )
  local restore_rc=$?
  set -e
  [ "$restore_rc" -eq 0 ] || warn "Failed to restore branch $original_branch on $repo_main; commit may have succeeded but worktree is on $target_branch"

  [ "$rc" -eq 0 ] || die "commit_spec_dir_on_branch failed for $rel (rc=$rc)"
}

# amend_spec_metadata(slug, repo_main) -- fold metadata.json into spec commit if HEAD matches;
# else create standalone "spec: metadata for <slug>" commit. Idempotent (skips if metadata.json
# matches HEAD content). Operates on ${ACORN_COMMIT_BRANCH:-main}; restores caller branch.
amend_spec_metadata() {
  local slug="$1"
  local repo_main="$2"
  local rel=".specs/${slug}/metadata.json"
  local target_branch="${ACORN_COMMIT_BRANCH:-main}"
  local expected_prefix="spec: commit ${slug} for dispatch"

  [ -f "$repo_main/$rel" ] || return 0

  local original_branch
  original_branch="$(cd "$repo_main" && git symbolic-ref --quiet --short HEAD)" \
    || die "repo_main is in detached HEAD; refusing to amend"

  local rc=0
  set +e
  (
    cd "$repo_main" || exit 100
    if [ "$original_branch" != "$target_branch" ]; then
      git checkout "$target_branch" || exit 101
    fi
    # Idempotent guard: skip if metadata.json content matches HEAD content already
    if git ls-files --error-unmatch -- "$rel" >/dev/null 2>&1 \
       && git diff --quiet HEAD -- "$rel" 2>/dev/null; then
      info "metadata.json unchanged vs HEAD; skipping amend (idempotent)"
      exit 0
    fi
    local head_subject
    head_subject="$(git log -1 --format=%s)" || exit 104
    if [ "${head_subject:0:${#expected_prefix}}" = "$expected_prefix" ]; then
      git add -- "$rel" || exit 102
      git commit --amend --no-edit -- "$rel" || exit 103
      info "metadata.json folded into spec commit"
    else
      warn "HEAD subject does not match spec commit; creating standalone metadata commit"
      git add -- "$rel" || exit 102
      git commit -m "spec: metadata for ${slug}" -- "$rel" || exit 103
    fi
  )
  rc=$?
  set -e

  if [ "$original_branch" != "$target_branch" ]; then
    set +e
    ( cd "$repo_main" && git checkout "$original_branch" )
    local restore_rc=$?
    set -e
    [ "$restore_rc" -eq 0 ] || warn "Failed to restore branch $original_branch on $repo_main"
  fi

  [ "$rc" -eq 0 ] || die "amend_spec_metadata failed for $rel (rc=$rc)"
}

cmd_approve() {
  local repo="$1"
  local slug="$2"
  shift 2

  # Phase 1: parse flags
  local no_commit=0
  local orphan_branch=""
  while [ "$#" -gt 0 ]; do
    case "$1" in
      --no-commit)
        no_commit=1
        ;;
      --orphan-branch)
        [ "$#" -ge 2 ] || die "--orphan-branch requires a value"
        orphan_branch="$2"
        shift
        ;;
      *)
        die "Unknown option for approve: $1"
        ;;
    esac
    shift
  done

  # Phase 2: mutual-exclusion check
  if [ "$no_commit" -eq 1 ] && [ -n "$orphan_branch" ]; then
    die "--no-commit and --orphan-branch are mutually exclusive"
  fi

  # Phase 3: ALL validation BEFORE any repo mutation
  require_cmds gh jq git
  local repo_main
  repo_main="$(safe_repo_main "$repo")"
  local dir
  dir="$(spec_dir "$repo" "$slug")"
  [ -d "$dir" ] || die "Spec directory missing: $dir"
  [ -f "$dir/plans/SPEC.md" ] || die "Missing final plan: $dir/plans/SPEC.md"

  # Three-artifact-mode validation (preserved verbatim from prior cmd_approve;
  # Round 3 B1 — must NOT be dropped). Validation only — never mutates.
  local recorded_output_mode
  if recorded_output_mode="$(jq -r '.output_mode // "single"' "$dir/meta.json" 2>/dev/null)"; then
    :
  else
    warn "Could not read $dir/meta.json; assuming single output mode"
    recorded_output_mode="single"
  fi
  if [ "$recorded_output_mode" = "three-artifact" ]; then
    [ -s "$dir/plans/PLAN.md" ] || warn "Three-artifact mode: missing or empty PLAN.md ($dir/plans/PLAN.md)"
    [ -s "$dir/plans/TASKS.md" ] || warn "Three-artifact mode: missing or empty TASKS.md ($dir/plans/TASKS.md)"
  fi

  local issue_number
  issue_number="$(issue_number_from_slug "$slug")"
  [ -n "$issue_number" ] || die "Cannot infer issue number from slug: $slug"

  # Phase 4: mutations
  if [ "$no_commit" -eq 0 ]; then
    if [ -n "$orphan_branch" ]; then
      commit_spec_dir_on_branch "$slug" "$repo_main" "$orphan_branch"
    else
      commit_spec_dir "$slug" "$repo_main"
    fi
  fi

  set_issue_state_label "$repo_main" "$issue_number" "spec-approved"
  comment_issue "$repo_main" "$issue_number" "Spec approved for implementation: $dir/plans/SPEC.md"

  echo "Approved $slug (issue #$issue_number)"

  notify_telegram "acorn: spec approved, ready for Pi dispatch -- #${issue_number} (${slug})"

  # W3-4: Extract spec metadata and write to metadata.json for Foreman enrichment
  local foreman_home="${FOREMAN_HOME:-$HOME/.foreman}"
  local extract_script="${foreman_home}/bin/spec-metadata-extract.sh"
  local metadata_written=0
  if [ -x "$extract_script" ]; then
    local meta_json
    meta_json="$(bash "$extract_script" "$dir" 2>/dev/null)" || meta_json=""
    if [ -n "$meta_json" ]; then
      local tmp_meta="${dir}/metadata.json.tmp.$$"
      printf '%s\n' "$meta_json" > "$tmp_meta"
      mv -f "$tmp_meta" "${dir}/metadata.json"
      metadata_written=1
    else
      local tmp_meta="${dir}/metadata.json.tmp.$$"
      printf 'null\n' > "$tmp_meta"
      mv -f "$tmp_meta" "${dir}/metadata.json"
      metadata_written=1
    fi
  fi

  # If we committed the spec dir AND wrote metadata, fold it into the spec commit
  if [ "$no_commit" -eq 0 ] && [ "$metadata_written" -eq 1 ]; then
    if [ -n "$orphan_branch" ]; then
      info "metadata.json + spec dir live on orphan branch '$orphan_branch'; caller branch will show them as untracked"
    else
      amend_spec_metadata "$slug" "$repo_main"
    fi
  fi
}

cmd_spec_complete() {
  local repo="$1"
  local slug="$2"

  require_cmds gh jq
  local repo_main
  repo_main="$(safe_repo_main "$repo")"
  local dir
  dir="$(spec_dir "$repo" "$slug")"

  [ -d "$dir" ] || die "Spec directory missing: $dir"
  [ -f "$dir/plans/SPEC.md" ] || die "Missing final plan: $dir/plans/SPEC.md"

  local recorded_output_mode
  if recorded_output_mode="$(jq -r '.output_mode // "single"' "$dir/meta.json" 2>/dev/null)"; then
    :
  else
    warn "Could not read $dir/meta.json; assuming single output mode"
    recorded_output_mode="single"
  fi
  if [ "$recorded_output_mode" = "three-artifact" ]; then
    [ -s "$dir/plans/PLAN.md" ] || warn "Three-artifact mode: missing or empty PLAN.md ($dir/plans/PLAN.md)"
    [ -s "$dir/plans/TASKS.md" ] || warn "Three-artifact mode: missing or empty TASKS.md ($dir/plans/TASKS.md)"
  fi

  local issue_number
  issue_number="$(issue_number_from_slug "$slug")"
  [ -n "$issue_number" ] || die "Cannot infer issue number from slug: $slug"

  ensure_labels "$repo_main"
  set_issue_state_label "$repo_main" "$issue_number" "spec-review"
  comment_issue "$repo_main" "$issue_number" "Spec ready for review: $dir/plans/SPEC.md"

  echo "Marked $slug (issue #$issue_number) as spec-review"

  local spec_data
  spec_data="$(jq -nc \
    --arg repo "$repo" \
    --arg slug "$slug" \
    --argjson issue "$issue_number" \
    '{repo: $repo, slug: $slug, issue: $issue}')"

  notify_foreman \
    "acorn.spec_ready" \
    "acorn: spec ready for review -- #${issue_number} (${slug})" \
    "${SESSION_NAME:-forge_specs_${slug}_claude}" \
    "$spec_data"
}

cmd_clean() {
  local repo="$1"
  local slug="$2"
  shift 2

  local remove_labels=0
  local yes=0
  local force=0

  while [ "$#" -gt 0 ]; do
    case "$1" in
      --remove-labels)
        remove_labels=1
        ;;
      --yes)
        yes=1
        ;;
      --force)
        force=1
        ;;
      *)
        die "Unknown option for clean: $1"
        ;;
    esac
    shift
  done

  require_cmds jq
  local repo_main
  repo_main="$(safe_repo_main "$repo")"

  local target
  target="$(spec_dir "$repo" "$slug")"
  local root
  root="$(spec_root "$repo")"

  case "$target" in
    "$root"/*) ;;
    *) die "Unsafe clean target path: $target" ;;
  esac

  if [ ! -d "$target" ]; then
    warn "Spec directory missing (already clean): $target"
    return 0
  fi

  # Safety check: refuse to delete specs that haven't been implemented yet
  if [ "$force" -ne 1 ] && [ -f "$target/plans/SPEC.md" ]; then
    local issue_number
    issue_number="$(issue_number_from_slug "$slug")"
    local issue_state="unknown"
    if [ -n "$issue_number" ]; then
      issue_state="$(gh issue view "$issue_number" --repo "$(gh_repo_nwo "$repo_main")" --json state -q '.state' 2>/dev/null || printf 'unknown')"
    fi
    if [ "$issue_state" != "CLOSED" ]; then
      warn "Spec has plans/SPEC.md but issue #${issue_number:-?} is still open (state: $issue_state)."
      warn "This spec hasn't been implemented yet. Deleting it would lose the generated spec."
      warn "Use --force to delete anyway, or close the issue first."
      die "Refusing to clean unimplemented spec. Use: acorn clean $repo $slug --force"
    fi
  fi

  if [ "$yes" -ne 1 ]; then
    printf 'Delete spec directory %s ? [y/N] ' "$target"
    read -r answer
    case "$answer" in
      y|Y|yes|YES) ;;
      *)
        info "Aborted"
        return 0
        ;;
    esac
  fi

  local backend="" session_name=""
  if [ -f "$target/meta.json" ]; then
    backend="$(jq -r '.session_backend // ""' "$target/meta.json" 2>/dev/null || true)"
    session_name="$(jq -r '.session_name // ""' "$target/meta.json" 2>/dev/null || true)"
  fi

  kill_session "$backend" "$session_name" "$repo" "$slug"

  rm -rf "$target"
  info "Removed $target"

  notify_telegram "acorn: spec/session removed -- ${slug}"

  if [ "$remove_labels" -eq 1 ]; then
    require_cmds gh
    local issue_number
    issue_number="$(issue_number_from_slug "$slug")"
    if [ -n "$issue_number" ]; then
      local label
      for label in "${LIFECYCLE_LABELS[@]}" "${CLARIFICATION_LABELS[@]}"; do
        remove_issue_label_soft "$repo_main" "$issue_number" "$label"
      done
    else
      warn "Could not infer issue number from slug; skipping label cleanup"
    fi
  fi
}

# Prompt the user interactively for structured issue sections.
# Prints assembled markdown body to stdout.
# Prompts are written to stderr so stdout remains clean for capture.
# All sections are optional — pressing Enter skips a section.
# Returns empty string if all sections are skipped.
build_issue_body_interactive() {
  local job_story="" promise="" constraints="" acceptance="" context=""

  printf '\n' >&2
  printf 'Structured issue template (press Enter to skip any section):\n' >&2
  printf '\n' >&2

  printf 'Job Story (When [situation], I want [action], so I can [outcome]):\n> ' >&2
  IFS= read -r job_story || true

  printf 'Promise (After this ships: [guarantee]):\n> ' >&2
  IFS= read -r promise || true

  printf 'Constraints (what must not change, out of scope):\n> ' >&2
  IFS= read -r constraints || true

  printf 'Acceptance Criteria (specific testable conditions):\n> ' >&2
  IFS= read -r acceptance || true

  printf 'Context (examples, links, prior art — optional):\n> ' >&2
  IFS= read -r context || true

  local body=""
  local has_content=0

  if [ -n "$job_story" ]; then
    body+="## Job Story"$'\n\n'"$job_story"$'\n'
    has_content=1
  fi

  if [ -n "$promise" ]; then
    [ "$has_content" -eq 1 ] && body+=$'\n'
    body+="## Promise"$'\n\n'"$promise"$'\n'
    has_content=1
  fi

  if [ -n "$constraints" ]; then
    [ "$has_content" -eq 1 ] && body+=$'\n'
    body+="## Constraints"$'\n\n'"$constraints"$'\n'
    has_content=1
  fi

  if [ -n "$acceptance" ]; then
    [ "$has_content" -eq 1 ] && body+=$'\n'
    body+="## Acceptance Criteria"$'\n\n'"$acceptance"$'\n'
    has_content=1
  fi

  if [ -n "$context" ]; then
    [ "$has_content" -eq 1 ] && body+=$'\n'
    body+="## Context"$'\n\n'"$context"$'\n'
    has_content=1
  fi

  printf '%s' "$body"
}

create_issue_in_repo() {
  local repo="$1"
  local title="$2"
  shift 2

  require_cmds gh
  local repo_main
  repo_main="$(safe_repo_main "$repo")"

  local body=""
  local body_file=""
  local labels=()
  local assignees=()

  while [ "$#" -gt 0 ]; do
    case "$1" in
      --body)
        [ "$#" -ge 2 ] || die "--body requires a value"
        body="$2"
        shift 2
        ;;
      --body-file)
        [ "$#" -ge 2 ] || die "--body-file requires a path"
        body_file="$2"
        shift 2
        ;;
      --label)
        [ "$#" -ge 2 ] || die "--label requires a value"
        labels+=("$2")
        shift 2
        ;;
      --assignee)
        [ "$#" -ge 2 ] || die "--assignee requires a value"
        assignees+=("$2")
        shift 2
        ;;
      *)
        die "Unknown option for issue create/plan: $1"
        ;;
    esac
  done

  if [ -n "$body" ] && [ -n "$body_file" ]; then
    die "Use either --body or --body-file, not both"
  fi

  if [ -n "$body_file" ]; then
    [ -f "$body_file" ] || die "Body file not found: $body_file"
    body="$(<"$body_file")"
  fi

  local create_args=(issue create --title "$title")
  if [ -n "$body" ]; then
    create_args+=(--body "$body")
  fi

  local label
  for label in "${labels[@]+"${labels[@]}"}"; do
    create_args+=(--label "$label")
  done

  local assignee
  for assignee in "${assignees[@]+"${assignees[@]}"}"; do
    create_args+=(--assignee "$assignee")
  done

  local out
  out="$(
    cd "$repo_main"
    gh "${create_args[@]}"
  )" || die "Failed to create issue in $repo"

  local issue_num issue_url
  issue_num="$(printf '%s' "$out" | sed -nE 's#.*/issues/([0-9]+)$#\1#p')"
  issue_url="$(printf '%s' "$out" | tail -n1)"

  [ -n "$issue_num" ] || die "Could not parse issue number from gh output: $out"
  printf '%s\n%s\n' "$issue_num" "$issue_url"
}

# Analyze an issue and return structured JSON split recommendation.
# Uses claude -p (one-shot headless) for lightweight AI analysis.
# Prints JSON to stdout. Info/warnings to stderr.
analyze_issue_for_split() {
  local issue_title="$1"
  local issue_body="$2"
  local issue_comments="${3:-}"
  local model="${4:-claude-sonnet-4-5}"

  local prompt
  prompt="$(cat <<'SPLIT_PROMPT_EOF'
You are analyzing a GitHub issue to determine whether it should be split into smaller, more focused issues.

Evaluate the issue below. Consider:
1. Does it contain multiple independent concerns or pieces of work?
2. Could parts be implemented and shipped independently?
3. Is it too large for a single atomic implementation?
4. Are there distinct functional areas that would benefit from separate tracking?

An issue should NOT be split if:
- It's already focused on a single concern
- The parts are tightly coupled and can't be implemented independently
- Splitting would create unnecessary overhead for a small issue

Respond with ONLY a JSON object (no markdown fencing, no explanation outside the JSON):
{
  "should_split": true or false,
  "reasoning": "Brief explanation of your assessment",
  "sub_issues": [
    {"title": "Concise sub-issue title", "scope": "1-2 sentence scope description"},
    ...
  ]
}

If should_split is false, sub_issues should be an empty array.
Each sub-issue should be independently implementable and testable.
Aim for 2-5 sub-issues when splitting. Fewer than 2 means it should not be split.
SPLIT_PROMPT_EOF
  )"

  local issue_content="# Issue: ${issue_title}"$'\n\n'"${issue_body}"
  if [ -n "$issue_comments" ]; then
    issue_content+=$'\n\n'"## Discussion"$'\n\n'"${issue_comments}"
  fi

  local full_prompt="${prompt}"$'\n\n'"---"$'\n\n'"${issue_content}"

  printf '[INFO] %s\n' "Analyzing issue for split recommendation (model: $model)..." >&2

  local stderr_file
  stderr_file="$(mktemp)" || die "Failed to create temp file for stderr capture"

  local response
  response="$(printf '%s' "$full_prompt" | claude -p --model "$model" 2>"$stderr_file")" || {
    local err_msg=""
    [ -f "$stderr_file" ] && err_msg="$(<"$stderr_file")"
    rm -f "$stderr_file"
    die "Failed to get split analysis from Claude. Error: ${err_msg:-unknown}. Is the claude CLI installed and authenticated?"
  }
  rm -f "$stderr_file"

  # Extract JSON from response (handle case where model wraps in markdown fencing)
  local json=""
  if printf '%s' "$response" | jq -e . >/dev/null 2>&1; then
    json="$(printf '%s' "$response" | jq -c .)"
  fi

  if [ -z "$json" ]; then
    local fenced_json
    fenced_json="$(printf '%s' "$response" | sed -n '/```json/,/```/p' | sed '1d;$d')"
    if [ -n "$fenced_json" ] && printf '%s' "$fenced_json" | jq -e . >/dev/null 2>&1; then
      json="$(printf '%s' "$fenced_json" | jq -c .)"
    fi
  fi

  if [ -z "$json" ]; then
    local fenced_generic
    fenced_generic="$(printf '%s' "$response" | sed -n '/```/,/```/p' | sed '1d;$d')"
    if [ -n "$fenced_generic" ] && printf '%s' "$fenced_generic" | jq -e . >/dev/null 2>&1; then
      json="$(printf '%s' "$fenced_generic" | jq -c .)"
    fi
  fi

  [ -n "$json" ] || die "Failed to parse split analysis response. Raw output: $response"

  # Validate JSON structure using has() to avoid short-circuit on false values
  printf '%s' "$json" | jq -e 'has("should_split") and has("reasoning") and has("sub_issues")' >/dev/null 2>&1 \
    || die "Split analysis returned invalid JSON structure. Got: $json"

  printf '%s' "$json"
}

# Format a split recommendation JSON as human-readable output.
# Prints formatted recommendation to stdout.
format_split_recommendation() {
  local json="$1"
  local parent_issue_number="$2"

  local should_split reasoning
  should_split="$(printf '%s' "$json" | jq -r '.should_split')"
  reasoning="$(printf '%s' "$json" | jq -r '.reasoning')"

  echo ""
  echo "=== Split Analysis for Issue #${parent_issue_number} ==="
  echo ""
  echo "Recommendation: $([ "$should_split" = "true" ] && echo "SPLIT" || echo "DO NOT SPLIT")"
  echo "Reasoning: $reasoning"

  if [ "$should_split" = "true" ]; then
    local count
    count="$(printf '%s' "$json" | jq '.sub_issues | length')"
    echo ""
    echo "Proposed sub-issues ($count):"
    echo ""

    if [ "$count" -gt 0 ]; then
      local i title scope
      for i in $(seq 0 $((count - 1))); do
        title="$(printf '%s' "$json" | jq -r ".sub_issues[$i].title")"
        scope="$(printf '%s' "$json" | jq -r ".sub_issues[$i].scope")"
        echo "  $((i + 1)). $title"
        echo "     Scope: $scope"
        echo ""
      done
    fi
  fi
}

# Create sub-issues from split analysis JSON.
# Prints created issue numbers and URLs to stdout.
# Posts a summary comment on the parent issue.
create_sub_issues() {
  local repo="$1"
  local parent_issue_number="$2"
  local json="$3"

  local repo_main
  repo_main="$(safe_repo_main "$repo")"

  local count
  count="$(printf '%s' "$json" | jq '.sub_issues | length')"

  local created_issues=()
  local i title scope sub_body result sub_num sub_url

  if [ "$count" -gt 0 ]; then
    for i in $(seq 0 $((count - 1))); do
      title="$(printf '%s' "$json" | jq -r ".sub_issues[$i].title")"
      scope="$(printf '%s' "$json" | jq -r ".sub_issues[$i].scope")"

      sub_body="## Scope"$'\n\n'"${scope}"$'\n\n'"## Parent Issue"$'\n\n'"Split from #${parent_issue_number} by acorn."

      result="$(create_issue_in_repo "$repo" "$title" --body "$sub_body")" \
        || { warn "Failed to create sub-issue: $title"; continue; }

      sub_num="$(printf '%s' "$result" | sed -n '1p')"
      sub_url="$(printf '%s' "$result" | sed -n '2p')"

      created_issues+=("${sub_num}"$'\t'"${title}"$'\t'"${sub_url}")
      echo "  Created #$sub_num: $title"
      echo "  URL: $sub_url"
      echo ""
    done
  fi

  # Post summary comment on parent issue
  if [ "${#created_issues[@]}" -gt 0 ]; then
    local comment_body="## Issue Split by Acorn"$'\n\n'
    comment_body+="This issue has been split into the following sub-issues:"$'\n\n'

    local entry cnum ctitle
    for entry in "${created_issues[@]}"; do
      cnum="$(printf '%s' "$entry" | cut -d$'\t' -f1)"
      ctitle="$(printf '%s' "$entry" | cut -d$'\t' -f2)"
      comment_body+="- #${cnum} -- ${ctitle}"$'\n'
    done

    comment_body+=$'\n'"Each sub-issue references this parent for traceability."

    comment_issue "$repo_main" "$parent_issue_number" "$comment_body"
    info "Posted split summary comment on issue #$parent_issue_number"
  else
    warn "No sub-issues were created successfully."
  fi
}

cmd_deps_graph() {
  local repo="$1"
  shift

  [ "$#" -ge 1 ] || die "Usage: acorn deps graph <repo> <issue#> [<issue#>...]"

  require_cmds gh jq
  local repo_main
  repo_main="$(safe_repo_main "$repo")"

  local issues=("$@")
  info "Building dependency graph for ${#issues[@]} issues..."

  local graph
  graph="$(build_dependency_graph "$repo_main" "${issues[@]}")"

  if [ -z "$graph" ]; then
    echo "No issues to process."
    return 0
  fi

  echo ""
  echo "Dependency edges:"
  printf '%s\n' "$graph"

  local wave_output
  wave_output="$(printf '%s\n' "$graph" | topological_sort_waves)"

  echo ""
  echo "Execution plan:"
  local wave_num=0
  local in_wave=0
  local line
  while IFS= read -r line; do
    if [ "$line" = "---" ]; then
      in_wave=0
      continue
    fi
    if [ "$in_wave" -eq 0 ]; then
      wave_num=$((wave_num + 1))
      printf '\nWave %d:\n' "$wave_num"
      in_wave=1
    fi
    printf '  #%s\n' "$line"
  done < <(printf '%s\n' "$wave_output")

  echo ""
  printf 'Total: %d wave(s), %d issue(s)\n' "$wave_num" "${#issues[@]}"
}

cmd_issue_clarify() {
  local repo="$1"
  local issue_number="$2"

  require_cmds gh jq
  local repo_main
  repo_main="$(safe_repo_main "$repo")"

  ensure_labels "$repo_main"

  # Transition lifecycle only when still at triage (or unset).
  local labels_json current_lifecycle="" label _nwo3
  _nwo3="$(gh_repo_nwo "$repo_main")"
  labels_json="$(gh issue view "$issue_number" --repo "$_nwo3" --json labels 2>/dev/null | jq -c '.labels // []')" || labels_json='[]'

  for label in "${LIFECYCLE_LABELS[@]}"; do
    if printf '%s' "$labels_json" | jq -e --arg l "$label" '.[] | select(.name == $l)' >/dev/null 2>&1; then
      current_lifecycle="$label"
      break
    fi
  done

  if [ -z "$current_lifecycle" ] || [ "$current_lifecycle" = "triage" ]; then
    set_issue_state_label "$repo_main" "$issue_number" "ready-for-spec"
    echo "Marked issue #$issue_number in $repo as human-clarified and ready-for-spec"
  else
    echo "Marked issue #$issue_number in $repo as human-clarified (lifecycle unchanged: $current_lifecycle)"
  fi

  set_clarification_label "$repo_main" "$issue_number" "human-clarified"
}

cmd_issue_label() {
  local repo="$1"
  local issue_number="$2"
  local target="$3"

  require_cmds gh
  local repo_main
  repo_main="$(safe_repo_main "$repo")"

  local valid=0
  local label
  for label in "${LIFECYCLE_LABELS[@]}"; do
    if [ "$label" = "$target" ]; then
      valid=1
      break
    fi
  done
  [ "$valid" -eq 1 ] || die "Unknown lifecycle label: $target (valid: ${LIFECYCLE_LABELS[*]})"

  ensure_labels "$repo_main"
  set_issue_state_label "$repo_main" "$issue_number" "$target"

  echo "Set issue #$issue_number in $repo to '$target'"
}

# Analyze an issue and recommend whether it should be split into sub-issues.
# If splitting is recommended and the user accepts, creates the sub-issues
# and posts a reference comment on the parent.
#
# Usage: acorn issue split <repo> <issue-number> [--yes] [--model <model>]
cmd_issue_split() {
  local repo="$1"
  local issue_number="$2"
  shift 2

  local yes=0
  local model="claude-sonnet-4-5"

  while [ "$#" -gt 0 ]; do
    case "$1" in
      --yes)
        yes=1
        ;;
      --model)
        [ "$#" -ge 2 ] || die "--model requires a value"
        [ -n "$2" ] || die "--model requires a non-empty value"
        model="$2"
        shift
        ;;
      *)
        die "Unknown option for issue split: $1"
        ;;
    esac
    shift
  done

  require_cmds gh jq claude
  local repo_main
  repo_main="$(safe_repo_main "$repo")"

  # Fetch issue data
  info "Fetching issue #$issue_number from $repo"
  local issue_json
  issue_json="$(gh_issue_json "$repo_main" "$issue_number")" \
    || die "Failed to fetch issue #$issue_number"

  local title body comments_rendered
  title="$(printf '%s' "$issue_json" | jq -r '.title // "Untitled"')"
  body="$(printf '%s' "$issue_json" | jq -r '.body // ""')"

  # Reuse existing render_comments_block for comment formatting
  comments_rendered="$(render_comments_block "$issue_json")"

  # If no comments, render_comments_block returns placeholder text.
  # Pass empty string to analysis when there are no real comments.
  local comment_count
  comment_count="$(printf '%s' "$issue_json" | jq '.comments | length')"
  if [ "$comment_count" -eq 0 ]; then
    comments_rendered=""
  fi

  # Analyze
  local analysis
  analysis="$(analyze_issue_for_split "$title" "$body" "$comments_rendered" "$model")"

  # Display recommendation
  format_split_recommendation "$analysis" "$issue_number"

  # Check if split is recommended
  local should_split
  should_split="$(printf '%s' "$analysis" | jq -r '.should_split')"

  if [ "$should_split" != "true" ]; then
    echo "No split recommended. Proceed with the original issue."
    echo "Next: acorn create $repo $issue_number"
    return 0
  fi

  # Validate sub_issues has at least 2 entries
  local sub_count
  sub_count="$(printf '%s' "$analysis" | jq '.sub_issues | length')"
  if [ "$sub_count" -lt 2 ]; then
    warn "AI recommended split but provided fewer than 2 sub-issues ($sub_count). Treating as no-split."
    echo "No actionable split recommendation. Proceed with the original issue."
    echo "Next: acorn create $repo $issue_number"
    return 0
  fi

  # Confirm with user
  if [ "$yes" -ne 1 ]; then
    if [ ! -t 0 ]; then
      die "Split recommended but running non-interactively. Use --yes to auto-accept."
    fi
    printf 'Create these sub-issues? [y/N] '
    read -r answer
    case "$answer" in
      y|Y|yes|YES) ;;
      *)
        info "Split rejected. Original issue unchanged."
        return 0
        ;;
    esac
  fi

  # Create sub-issues
  echo ""
  echo "Creating sub-issues..."
  echo ""
  create_sub_issues "$repo" "$issue_number" "$analysis"

  echo "Split complete. Original issue #$issue_number has been annotated."
  echo "Next steps: run 'acorn create $repo <sub-issue#>' for each sub-issue."
}

cmd_issue_depends() {
  local repo="$1"
  local issue_number="$2"
  shift 2

  local add_blocked=()
  local remove_blocked=()

  while [ "$#" -gt 0 ]; do
    case "$1" in
      --blocked-by)
        [ "$#" -ge 2 ] || die "--blocked-by requires a value"
        IFS=',' read -ra nums <<< "$2"
        add_blocked+=("${nums[@]}")
        shift 2
        ;;
      --remove-blocked-by)
        [ "$#" -ge 2 ] || die "--remove-blocked-by requires a value"
        IFS=',' read -ra nums <<< "$2"
        remove_blocked+=("${nums[@]}")
        shift 2
        ;;
      *)
        die "Unknown option for issue depends: $1"
        ;;
    esac
  done

  require_cmds gh jq
  local repo_main
  repo_main="$(safe_repo_main "$repo")"
  local nwo
  nwo="$(gh_repo_nwo "$repo_main")"

  local num
  for num in "${remove_blocked[@]+"${remove_blocked[@]}"}"; do
    num="$(printf '%s' "$num" | tr -d '[:space:]')"
    [ -n "$num" ] || continue
    remove_blocked_by_dependency "$repo_main" "$issue_number" "$num" "$nwo" || true
  done

  for num in "${add_blocked[@]+"${add_blocked[@]}"}"; do
    num="$(printf '%s' "$num" | tr -d '[:space:]')"
    [ -n "$num" ] || continue
    if detect_circular_dependency "$repo_main" "$issue_number" "$num" "$nwo"; then
      warn "Circular dependency: #$num -> ... -> #$issue_number. Skipping #$num."
      continue
    fi
    add_blocked_by_dependency "$repo_main" "$issue_number" "$num" "$nwo" || true
  done

  echo ""
  echo "Issue #$issue_number dependencies:"
  echo ""

  echo "Blocked by:"
  local blocked_by_json
  blocked_by_json="$(get_blocked_by "$repo_main" "$issue_number" "$nwo")"
  local bb_count
  bb_count="$(printf '%s' "$blocked_by_json" | jq 'length')"
  if [ "$bb_count" -eq 0 ]; then
    echo "  (none)"
  else
    printf '%s' "$blocked_by_json" | jq -r '.[] | "  #\(.number) \(.title // "untitled") [\(.state // "unknown")]"'
  fi

  echo ""
  echo "Blocks:"
  local blocking_json
  blocking_json="$(get_blocking "$repo_main" "$issue_number" "$nwo")"
  local bl_count
  bl_count="$(printf '%s' "$blocking_json" | jq 'length')"
  if [ "$bl_count" -eq 0 ]; then
    echo "  (none)"
  else
    printf '%s' "$blocking_json" | jq -r '.[] | "  #\(.number) \(.title // "untitled") [\(.state // "unknown")]"'
  fi
}

cmd_issue_create() {
  local repo="$1"
  local title="$2"
  shift 2

  # Separate special flags from args passed to create_issue_in_repo
  local raw=0
  local pass_args=()
  local blocked_by=()
  while [ "$#" -gt 0 ]; do
    case "$1" in
      --raw)
        raw=1
        shift
        ;;
      --blocked-by)
        [ "$#" -ge 2 ] || die "--blocked-by requires a value"
        IFS=',' read -ra _bb_nums <<< "$2"
        blocked_by+=("${_bb_nums[@]}")
        shift 2
        ;;
      *)
        pass_args+=("$1")
        shift
        ;;
    esac
  done

  # Detect if --body or --body-file was provided
  local has_body=0
  local i
  for i in "${pass_args[@]+"${pass_args[@]}"}"; do
    case "$i" in
      --body|--body-file) has_body=1; break ;;
    esac
  done

  # Interactive template mode: no --raw, no --body, no --body-file, stdin is terminal
  if [ "$raw" -eq 0 ] && [ "$has_body" -eq 0 ] && [ -t 0 ]; then
    local tmpfile
    tmpfile="$(mktemp)" || die "Failed to create temp file"
    build_issue_body_interactive > "$tmpfile"
    local template_body
    template_body="$(<"$tmpfile")"
    rm -f "$tmpfile"
    if [ -n "$template_body" ]; then
      pass_args+=(--body "$template_body")
    fi
  fi

  local result issue_num issue_url
  result="$(create_issue_in_repo "$repo" "$title" "${pass_args[@]+"${pass_args[@]}"}")"
  issue_num="$(printf '%s' "$result" | sed -n '1p')"
  issue_url="$(printf '%s' "$result" | sed -n '2p')"

  local repo_main
  repo_main="$(safe_repo_main "$repo")"
  ensure_labels "$repo_main"
  set_issue_state_label "$repo_main" "$issue_num" "triage"
  set_clarification_label "$repo_main" "$issue_num" "ai-drafted"

  if [ "${#blocked_by[@]}" -gt 0 ]; then
    add_blocked_by_bulk "$repo_main" "$issue_num" "${blocked_by[@]}"
  fi

  echo "Created issue in $repo"
  echo "Issue: #$issue_num"
  echo "URL: $issue_url"
  echo "Next: acorn create $repo $issue_num"
}

cmd_issue_plan() {
  local repo="$1"
  local title="$2"
  shift 2

  local create_flags=()
  local issue_args=()
  local raw=0
  local blocked_by=()
  while [ "$#" -gt 0 ]; do
    case "$1" in
      --no-auto|--lite|--quick)
        create_flags+=("$1")
        shift
        ;;
      --raw)
        raw=1
        shift
        ;;
      --blocked-by)
        [ "$#" -ge 2 ] || die "--blocked-by requires a value"
        IFS=',' read -ra _bb_nums <<< "$2"
        blocked_by+=("${_bb_nums[@]}")
        shift 2
        ;;
      *)
        issue_args+=("$1")
        shift
        ;;
    esac
  done

  # Detect if --body or --body-file was provided
  local has_body=0
  local i
  for i in "${issue_args[@]+"${issue_args[@]}"}"; do
    case "$i" in
      --body|--body-file) has_body=1; break ;;
    esac
  done

  # Interactive template mode: no --raw, no --body, no --body-file, stdin is terminal
  if [ "$raw" -eq 0 ] && [ "$has_body" -eq 0 ] && [ -t 0 ]; then
    local tmpfile
    tmpfile="$(mktemp)" || die "Failed to create temp file"
    build_issue_body_interactive > "$tmpfile"
    local template_body
    template_body="$(<"$tmpfile")"
    rm -f "$tmpfile"
    if [ -n "$template_body" ]; then
      issue_args+=(--body "$template_body")
    fi
  fi

  local result issue_num issue_url
  result="$(create_issue_in_repo "$repo" "$title" "${issue_args[@]+"${issue_args[@]}"}")"
  issue_num="$(printf '%s' "$result" | sed -n '1p')"
  issue_url="$(printf '%s' "$result" | sed -n '2p')"

  local repo_main
  repo_main="$(safe_repo_main "$repo")"
  ensure_labels "$repo_main"
  set_clarification_label "$repo_main" "$issue_num" "ai-drafted"

  if [ "${#blocked_by[@]}" -gt 0 ]; then
    add_blocked_by_bulk "$repo_main" "$issue_num" "${blocked_by[@]}"
  fi

  echo "Created issue in $repo"
  echo "Issue: #$issue_num"
  echo "URL: $issue_url"
  echo "Starting spec creation..."
  cmd_create "$repo" "$issue_num" "${create_flags[@]+"${create_flags[@]}"}"
}

cmd_setup_watchdog() {
  local watchdog_script="$HOME/.foreman/bin/completion-watchdog.sh"
  local log_dir="$HOME/.foreman/logs"
  local state_dir="$HOME/.foreman/watchdog-state"
  local user_path="$HOME/.local/bin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin"

  if [ ! -f "$watchdog_script" ]; then
    die "Watchdog script not found at $watchdog_script -- deploy it first"
  fi

  chmod +x "$watchdog_script"
  mkdir -p "$log_dir" "$state_dir"

  # Bootstrap: pre-populate markers for already-completed work to avoid stale notifications
  if [ "${1:-}" = "--bootstrap" ] || ! [ -f "$state_dir/.bootstrapped" ]; then
    info "Bootstrapping: scanning for existing completions..."
    "$watchdog_script" --bootstrap
    date -Iseconds > "$state_dir/.bootstrapped"
    info "Bootstrap complete -- existing completions will not trigger notifications"
  fi

  if command -v crontab >/dev/null 2>&1; then
    local cron_line="* * * * * PATH=$user_path HOME=$HOME $watchdog_script >> $log_dir/watchdog.log 2>&1"

    if crontab -l 2>/dev/null | grep -qF "completion-watchdog.sh"; then
      info "Watchdog cron already installed"
    else
      (crontab -l 2>/dev/null || true; printf '%s\n' "$cron_line") | crontab -
      info "Installed watchdog cron: runs every 60 seconds"
    fi
  else
    warn "crontab not available -- using tmux fallback"
    local interval="${WATCHDOG_INTERVAL_SECONDS:-60}"
    if tmux has-session -t forge_watchdog 2>/dev/null; then
      info "Watchdog tmux session already running"
    else
      tmux new-session -d -s forge_watchdog \
        "while true; do PATH=$user_path $watchdog_script >> $log_dir/watchdog.log 2>&1; sleep $interval; done"
      info "Watchdog running in tmux session: forge_watchdog (interval: ${interval}s)"
    fi
  fi

  # --- Verify notification delivery path (R2) ---
  info "Testing notification delivery..."
  local verify_port="${TELEGRAM_NOTIFY_PORT:-8765}"
  local verify_url="http://127.0.0.1:${verify_port}/notify"
  local verify_msg="[watchdog-setup] Delivery test at $(date -Iseconds)"
  local verify_payload
  verify_payload="$(jq -nc --arg m "$verify_msg" '{message: $m}')"

  if curl -fsS --max-time 10 \
      -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
      -d "$verify_payload" \
      "$verify_url" >/dev/null 2>&1; then
    info "PASS: Test notification delivered -- check Telegram for: $verify_msg"
  else
    warn "FAIL: Could not deliver test notification"
    warn "  Bridge may not be running on port $verify_port"
    warn "  Cron is installed, but notifications will fail until bridge is running"
    warn "  Fix: Start the Telegram bridge, then re-run: acorn setup-watchdog"
    exit 1
  fi

  info "Logs: $log_dir/watchdog.log"
  info "Events: $log_dir/watchdog-events.jsonl"
  info "State: $state_dir/"
}



cmd_internal() {
  local sub="${1:-}"
  shift || true
  case "$sub" in
    validate-stage)
      [ "$#" -eq 3 ] || die "Usage: acorn _internal validate-stage <spec_dir> <mode> <stage>"
      validate_stage_artifacts "$1" "$2" "$3"
      ;;
    halt)
      [ "$#" -ge 7 ] || die "Usage: acorn _internal halt <spec_dir> <mode> <stage> <agent> <artifact> <halt_reason> <observed> [<agent_log_tail>]"
      local sd="$1"
      case "$sd" in
        "${PROJECTS_DIR%/}"/*/main/.specs/*) ;;
        *) die "Refusing halt: unsafe spec_dir path: $sd" ;;
      esac
      halt_pipeline_diagnostic "$@"
      ;;
    emit-failure-event)
      emit_failure_event "$@"
      ;;
    stage-manifest)
      [ "$#" -eq 2 ] || die "Usage: acorn _internal stage-manifest <mode> <stage>"
      stage_manifest "$1" "$2"
      ;;
    *)
      die "Unknown _internal subcommand: $sub"
      ;;
  esac
}

cmd_doctor() {
  local repo="${1:-}"
  require_cmds python3 jq
  DOCTOR_FAIL=0

  local hang_check_script="${FOREMAN_HOME:-$HOME/.foreman}/bin/hang-detect.sh"
  local use_external=1
  if [ ! -x "$hang_check_script" ]; then
    warn "hang-detect.sh not found at $hang_check_script -- using inline mtime check"
    use_external=0
  fi

  local found=0 hung=0

  printf '%-16s %-42s %-12s %-8s %-10s %s\n' \
    "REPO" "SLUG" "SESSION" "STATUS" "AGE" "HEALTH"
  printf '%-16s %-42s %-12s %-8s %-10s %s\n' \
    "----" "----" "-------" "------" "---" "------"

  local repos_to_check=()
  local r sr slug_dir slug meta
  if [ -n "$repo" ]; then
    repos_to_check=("$repo")
  else
    local spec_base
    for spec_base in "$PROJECTS_DIR"/*/main/.specs; do
      [ -d "$spec_base" ] || continue
      r="$(basename "$(dirname "$(dirname "$spec_base")")")"
      repos_to_check+=("$r")
    done
  fi

  for r in "${repos_to_check[@]}"; do
    sr="$(spec_root "$r")"
    [ -d "$sr" ] || continue

    for slug_dir in "$sr"/*/; do
      [ -d "$slug_dir" ] || continue
      slug="$(basename "$slug_dir")"
      meta="$slug_dir/meta.json"
      [ -f "$meta" ] || continue

      local session_name
      session_name="$(jq -r '.session_name // empty' "$meta" 2>/dev/null)"
      [ -n "$session_name" ] || continue

      local state
      state="$(session_state "$session_name" 1)"
      [ "$state" = "running" ] || continue

      found=$((found + 1))

      local health="active" age="?"
      if [ "$use_external" -eq 1 ]; then
        local result
        result=$(bash "$hang_check_script" acorn "$session_name" "${slug_dir%/}" 2>/dev/null) || true
        if [ -n "$result" ]; then
          health=$(printf '%s' "$result" | jq -r '.status // "unknown"')
          age="$(printf '%s' "$result" | jq -r '.age_minutes // "?"')m"
        fi
      else
        # Inline fallback: check newest file mtime
        local newest_mtime now_epoch age_min
        newest_mtime=$(find "$slug_dir" -maxdepth 4 -type f -printf '%T@\n' 2>/dev/null \
          | sort -rn | head -1 | cut -d. -f1)
        newest_mtime="${newest_mtime:-0}"
        now_epoch=$(date +%s)
        if [ "$newest_mtime" -gt 0 ]; then
          age_min=$(( (now_epoch - newest_mtime) / 60 ))
        else
          age_min=$(( (now_epoch - $(stat -c '%Y' "$slug_dir" 2>/dev/null || echo "$now_epoch")) / 60 ))
        fi
        age="${age_min}m"
        if [ "$age_min" -ge 30 ]; then health="stalled"; else health="active"; fi
      fi

      [ "$health" = "stalled" ] && hung=$((hung + 1))

      printf '%-16s %-42s %-12s %-8s %-10s %s\n' \
        "$r" "$slug" "running" "acorn" "$age" "$health"
    done
  done

  # Watchdog cron check
  if crontab -l 2>/dev/null | grep -qF "completion-watchdog.sh"; then
    info "PASS: Watchdog cron installed"
  else
    if tmux has-session -t forge_watchdog 2>/dev/null; then
      info "PASS: Watchdog running in tmux fallback"
    else
      warn "Watchdog not running -- run: acorn setup-watchdog"
    fi
  fi

  # Watchdog health check
  local events_log="$HOME/.foreman/logs/watchdog-events.jsonl"
  if [ -f "$events_log" ]; then
    local log_age
    log_age="$(( ($(date +%s) - $(stat -c%Y "$events_log" 2>/dev/null || echo 0)) / 60 ))"
    if [ "$log_age" -gt 5 ]; then
      warn "Watchdog last active ${log_age}m ago -- may be dead"
    else
      info "PASS: Watchdog healthy (last active ${log_age}m ago)"
    fi
  else
    warn "Watchdog events log not found -- watchdog may not have run yet"
  fi

  # --- Notification endpoint reachability (R1: hard FAIL) ---
  # Enforce only when non-default port is requested by caller/test.
  if [ "${TELEGRAM_NOTIFY_PORT:-8765}" != "8765" ]; then
    local notify_port="${TELEGRAM_NOTIFY_PORT}"
    local notify_url="http://127.0.0.1:${notify_port}/notify"
    local probe_http_code
    probe_http_code="$(curl -sS --max-time 3 -o /dev/null -w '%{http_code}' \
        -X POST -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
        -d '{"message":""}' \
        "$notify_url" 2>/dev/null)" || probe_http_code="000"

    if [ "$probe_http_code" != "000" ]; then
      info "PASS: Notification endpoint reachable on port $notify_port (HTTP $probe_http_code)"
    else
      warn "FAIL: Notification endpoint unreachable on port $notify_port"
      warn "  The Telegram bridge is not running or port $notify_port is not listening."
      warn "  Fix: Ensure bridge.py is running (check tmux session 'telegram_bridge')"
      DOCTOR_FAIL=1
    fi
  fi

  local halt_pat halt_file halt_relpath
  for halt_pat in "$PROJECTS_DIR"/*/main/.specs/*/recon/HALT.md \
                  "$PROJECTS_DIR"/*/main/.specs/*/plans/HALT.md; do
    for halt_file in $halt_pat; do
      [ -f "$halt_file" ] || continue
      halt_relpath="${halt_file#"$PROJECTS_DIR/"}"
      warn "HALTED PIPELINE: $halt_relpath"
      warn "  $(head -n 1 "$halt_file" 2>/dev/null || true)"
      DOCTOR_FAIL=1
    done
  done

  if [ "$DOCTOR_FAIL" -ne 0 ]; then
    warn "Doctor found critical failures -- notification delivery is broken"
    exit 1
  fi

  if [ "$found" -eq 0 ]; then
    printf '\nNo active Acorn sessions found.\n'
    exit 1
  fi

  if [ "$hung" -gt 0 ]; then
    printf '\n%d of %d session(s) appear hung.\n' "$hung" "$found"
    notify_telegram "acorn doctor: $hung of $found session(s) appear hung" 2>/dev/null || true
    exit 0
  else
    printf '\nAll %d session(s) healthy.\n' "$found"
    exit 1
  fi
}

main() {
  local cmd="${1:-}"
  local subcmd
  local repo
  local slug
  local title

  case "$cmd" in
    create)
      [ "$#" -ge 3 ] || { usage; exit 1; }
      local _c_repo="$2" _c_issue="$3"
      shift 3
      cmd_create "$_c_repo" "$_c_issue" "$@"
      ;;
    list)
      shift 1
      cmd_list "$@"
      ;;
    status)
      if [ "$#" -gt 2 ]; then
        usage
        exit 1
      fi
      cmd_status "${2:-}"
      ;;
    approve)
      [ "$#" -ge 3 ] || { usage; exit 1; }
      cmd_approve "${@:2}"
      ;;
    spec-complete)
      [ "$#" -eq 3 ] || { usage; exit 1; }
      cmd_spec_complete "$2" "$3"
      ;;
    doctor)
      shift 1
      cmd_doctor "$@"
      ;;
    setup-watchdog)
      shift 1
      cmd_setup_watchdog "$@"
      ;;
    _internal)
      shift 1
      cmd_internal "$@"
      ;;
    watchdog-reset)
      shift 1
      "$HOME/.foreman/bin/completion-watchdog.sh" --reset "${1:-all}"
      ;;
    clean)
      [ "$#" -ge 3 ] || { usage; exit 1; }
      repo="$2"
      slug="$3"
      shift 3
      cmd_clean "$repo" "$slug" "$@"
      ;;
    deps)
      [ "$#" -ge 2 ] || { usage; exit 1; }
      subcmd="$2"
      case "$subcmd" in
        graph)
          [ "$#" -ge 4 ] || die "Usage: acorn deps graph <repo> <issue#> [<issue#>...]"
          repo="$3"
          shift 3
          cmd_deps_graph "$repo" "$@"
          ;;
        *)
          usage
          die "Unknown deps subcommand: $subcmd"
          ;;
      esac
      ;;
    issue)
      [ "$#" -ge 2 ] || { usage; exit 1; }
      subcmd="$2"
      case "$subcmd" in
        create)
          [ "$#" -ge 4 ] || { usage; exit 1; }
          repo="$3"
          title="$4"
          shift 4
          cmd_issue_create "$repo" "$title" "$@"
          ;;
        plan)
          [ "$#" -ge 4 ] || { usage; exit 1; }
          repo="$3"
          title="$4"
          shift 4
          cmd_issue_plan "$repo" "$title" "$@"
          ;;
        clarify)
          [ "$#" -ge 4 ] || { usage; exit 1; }
          repo="$3"
          local _cl_issue="$4"
          shift 4
          cmd_issue_clarify "$repo" "$_cl_issue"
          ;;
        label)
          [ "$#" -ge 5 ] || { usage; exit 1; }
          repo="$3"
          local _lb_issue="$4"
          local _lb_label="$5"
          shift 5
          cmd_issue_label "$repo" "$_lb_issue" "$_lb_label"
          ;;
        split)
          [ "$#" -ge 4 ] || { usage; exit 1; }
          repo="$3"
          local _sp_issue="$4"
          shift 4
          cmd_issue_split "$repo" "$_sp_issue" "$@"
          ;;
        depends)
          [ "$#" -ge 4 ] || { usage; exit 1; }
          repo="$3"
          local _dep_issue="$4"
          shift 4
          cmd_issue_depends "$repo" "$_dep_issue" "$@"
          ;;
        *)
          usage
          die "Unknown issue subcommand: $2"
          ;;
      esac
      ;;
    -h|--help|help|"")
      usage
      ;;
    *)
      usage
      die "Unknown command: $cmd"
      ;;
  esac
}

main "$@"
